drm/apple: ambient_matrix for the integrated panel's True Tone

macOS's CoreBrightness sets the panel's True Tone matrix at DCP matrix
location 9, independent of the compositor. Give the panel's DCP an
ambient_matrix attribute (nine signed 2^-32 units, row major; "0" drops it)
that is applied after the CRTC's CTM at that location, and push it with an
idle commit the way the backlight does, so a daemon (bakery-truetoned) can
ramp it at display rate.

The iomfb_template.c hunk has one line of trailing context on purpose: it
applies with and without patches/linux-vrr.

